Subject: [PATCH] stage 286: read each candidate from its own mentions, and
 stay inside the trunk's window

Two fixes, one of them mine and fatal to the point of the stage.

encode truncated to 256 BPE tokens while the trunk's positional table is
Embedding(MAX_ARCS, d) with MAX_ARCS 64, so a long enough evidence set
indexed past the table and the run died on the device. 271 truncates to
MAX_ARCS for exactly this reason and now so does this.

The larger one: the head pooled every mention into one vector and gave
the same vector to every candidate row. Such a reading cannot say which
candidate the text supports - it is constant across the softmax and can
only modulate how the counts are weighed - so the head would have been
votes and corroboration wearing a hat, and --no-hidden would have tied by
construction rather than by measurement. Each candidate is now read from
the mentions that carry it, cued with the subject, and UNKNOWN reads them
all. Verified on a hand tape that the rows and the readings align and
that each candidate sees only its own text.

Also stated plainly in the note what the stage is not: the address comes
from 280's plumbing, the candidates are what the evidence says, so the
ceiling here is what a correct address makes visible. This is about
weighing within the evidence set, nothing more.

